Retrieval over closed tickets (Phase 5A). When a ticket closes it becomes a document - what happened, and what was done about it - embedded into a pgvector corpus by a Job Hook. A **Similar Tickets** panel on an open ticket then shows the closest closed ones with their resolutions, so "somebody solved this in March and wrote it down" stops depending on who is awake. `services/rag.py` holds it (rules R1-R9), `services/llm.py::embed()` is the twin of `complete()` for the other kind of model call, and `nautobot-server indexclosedtickets` backfills a corpus that predates the feature. Off by default.
